		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4909&amp;p=35913#p35913"><![CDATA[
As discussed many times, there is no Chinese support in the firmware, as there are too many glyphs to support, requires multibytes strings and so on. The memory space is limited, and the strings are bytes based.<br>We have a kind of special string support, bitmap fonts and stuff like that.<br>Japanese have Katakana, which uses a limited set of glyph, but Chinese and Russian don't, hence it's not possible to support such languages (I know some Russians are using a kind of hack to support their language in a modified version of the firmware).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Feb 25, 2025 4:44 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
